            "SnowReport": {
                "LastUpdate": "2025-11-18T11:08:42-0500",
                "BaseConditions": "--",
                "Report": "<div>Our team of snowmakers is out on the mountain, taking advantage of every weather window they can get their gloves on. The efforts are starting to show on the Summit Webcam, with the first signs of whales appearing on the summit. Good snowmaking temperatures have allowed us to increase our efficiency and snowmaking footprint, including the lower mountain. We anticipate another great night of production tonight. Plus Mother Nature delivered 5 inches of snow in base overnight, and it's still coming down!<br><br></div><div>The Snowmaking team has stayed focused on Black Bear to Polar Bear, Mike's Way, Upper and Lower West Meadows, Drifter Link, Frank's Fall Line, Janeway Junction and Suntanner. We are closely monitoring base and summit temperatures and will keep you all in the loop if anything shifts.&nbsp; <br><br><strong>Stratton’s projected opening day</strong> for 2025-2026 is <a href=\"https://www.stratton.com/things-to-do/events/opening-day\">Wednesday, November 26</a>. Stay tuned to the event page and this Mountain Report, as this date is fluid and can change with the weather, but we’ll be sure to keep all of you eager skiers and riders updated for the upcoming winter season. Do your snow dances, ceremonial pajama rituals, and whatever else it may take to get Mother Nature to pitch in. We can’t wait to see you back on the slopes.<br><br><strong>Uphill Travel:</strong> We are proud to have an open, accommodating, and free-uphill policy, and that will remain in place. As always, your safety and our team's safety are our number one priority. With that, Uphill access at Stratton is <strong>temporarily suspended</strong> while we prepare the mountain for Opening Day. With snow guns roaring, crews moving about, no staffed Ski Patrol, and vehicles and equipment on the hill all in limited visibility, we ask that ALL hikers stay off the mountain at all times until further notice. Thank you for understanding. We want to ride as much as you do, so we ask that you take the extra time to prep your gear and get ready to ride rather than hiking at this time. We will update once uphill access is back open. Thank you, and let's have a great season.</div><div><br></div><div>Want to work at Stratton? Your next dream job is waiting for you in the mountains. Check out all of our open positions and benefits on the <a href=\"https://www.stratton.com/employment\">Stratton Employment page</a>.</div><div><br>Don't know when you're going to go? The <a href=\"https://www.ikonpass.com/en/local-passes/stratton/summit-saver-pass?webSyncID=b5879ac1-ae8d-de61-1b3a-2e8dd8ce96c3&amp;sessionGUID=c45c36b5-300d-5801-0271-685a9db6e0d1\">Stratton Summit Saver</a> is a flexible preloaded lift ticket, with your choice of 2, 3, or 4 tickets. The Summit Saver lets you go right to the lift and ride on your schedule, with pre-purchased, pre-loaded lift tickets on this RFID Pass. Did we mention NO blackout dates? Grab the Summit Saver starting at just $248 for adults and $196 for youth.<br><br>Time to lock in on your winter fun! Enroll in a high-performance adventure this season. This winter, accelerate your ability level through guided <a href=\"https://www.stratton.com/plan-your-trip/snowboarding-ski-lessons/seasonal-programs-camps\">seasonal programs</a> and specialty workshops with the Stratton Mountain Sports School. <a href=\"https://www.stratton.com/plan-your-trip/snowboarding-ski-lessons/seasonal-programs-camps\">Seasonal Programs</a> are the best way to turn your little one into a lifetime skier or snowboarder, with a strong foundation of skills, in a discipline they enjoy most. <a href=\"https://www.stratton.com/plan-your-trip/snowboarding-ski-lessons/seasonal-programs-camps\">Seasonal Programs</a> focus on fun at an early age, followed by specialty disciplines such as freestyle skiing and snowboarding, ski racing, freeriding, and more. These programs are offered for all ages, including adults, so it's never too late to join!<br><br><strong>Safety Tip:</strong> Be cautious of slippery and wet conditions!<strong> </strong>Temperatures at the summit may be much lower than the base area this time of year when hiking.<br><br>&nbsp;Stay and relish the Green Mountains! <a href=\"https://www.strattonrealestate.com/\">Stratton Real Estate</a> is here to help with all your real estate needs. Make your sweet escape a reality.<br><br>Reliable cars are the name of the game; that is why we trust Oliver Subaru and Ford. Made for all seasons and all families, check out <a href=\"https://www.oliverfordofbennington.com/\">Oliver Ford</a> and <a href=\"https://www.oliversubaruofrutland.com/\">Oliver Subaru</a> for year-round reliability!</div>",
